      "content": "thanks. i appreciate the discretion. okay, so here are a few from this morning. they seem so random but the timing is what's killing me.\n\n1. Subject: [URGENT] Q3 Risk Assessment - Updated Protocol\n2. Subject: Re: Wednesday Sync // Coffee? \n3. Subject: Internal Audit: Data Integrity Check (FYI ONLY)\n4. Subject: Meeting Request: Project Alpha - quick touch base\n\nthe thing is, every time i get one of these 'quick touch base' or 'FYI' emails, my supervisor or a peer from the compliance team suddenly starts looking at me or changes the subject in our next actual meeting. especially the one about 'Data Integrity'—it came right after i brought up the discrepancies in the hedge fund reporting. i'm starting to think they aren't just auditing the data, they're auditing *me*. can you look at these and tell me if there's a linguistic pattern or a specific sequence they're using to signal to each other when i'm being 'observed'?",
